      "title": "\ud83d\udcd6 Novice Analyst Guide: Port Scanning, Exfiltration & Payload Size Breakdown",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "transparent": true,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### \ud83d\udce4 Outbound Payload Transfer Classification & Network Exfiltration\n* **`< 1 KB` (Green - Normal):** Heartbeat signals, NTP time sync, DNS queries, telemetry ping.\n* **`1 KB - 500 KB` (Green - Normal):** Standard web page loading, API JSON data, small image assets.\n* **`500 KB - 10 MB` (Yellow - Elevated):** High-res photo downloads, audio streams, document syncs.\n* **`10 MB - 500 MB` (Orange - High Volume):** HD/4K Video streaming (YouTube/Netflix), OS/software updates.\n* **`> 500 MB` (Red - Critical Exfiltration Hazard):** Unencrypted database dumps, archive exfiltration, active malware C2 exfil ($Z > 3.0$ triggers immediate alert).\n* **Port Scans (S0/REJ):** Unanswered TCP connection requests. Spikes indicate port scanning / network discovery."
      }
